(4052405, 574569, 41337, '<td valign="top">Strange how some want this off-centered while others thought it was off-centered. How can this be? Looks centered enough for my tastes. Speaking of which, the centered composition couldn''t have been any more appropriate. It enhances the feeling of isolation. I also love how I can''t read what looks like words on the ground which is good because they are not meant for me.</td>', 'Strange how some want this off-centered while others thought it was off-centered. How can this be? Looks centered enough for my tastes. Speaking of which, the centered composition couldn''t have been any more appropriate. It enhances the feeling of isolation. I also love how I can''t read what looks like words on the ground which is good because they are not meant for me.', '2007-09-03 07:53:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4053219, 574545, 31403, '<td valign="top">don''t you love people here ramming their interpretation down your throat instead of appreciating the art for what it is?  What is it about the ability to comment that makes them think that''s acceptable?<br/> <br/>I think your message is loud and clear - the darkness of the image and the title speak very clearly to me - I appreciate your artistic uses of the tools, and I love the way your photos reflect your view of the world.  You communicate emotion in your work - a think many here will never grasp nor be able to do. <br/> <br/>Now get up there and delete that apology.  The fact they don''t agree with you does NOT make them any "righter" than you.  In fact, it makes them wrong in my book.  It''s your art, your execution, by definition you are right.  They can disagree with your "rightness" but it doesn''t make you "wrong".<br/> <br/>Sorry, I''ll put my righteous indignation away now.<br/> <br/>I don''t know how you feel about religion and God - if this reflects it or not - but He is one of my best friends.  I highly recommend getting to know Him in whatever way your heart leads you to.  :-)</td>', 'don''t you love people here ramming their interpretation down your throat instead of appreciating the art for what it is?  What is it about the ability to comment that makes them think that''s acceptable? I think your message is loud and clear - the darkness of the image and the title speak very clearly to me - I appreciate your artistic uses of the tools, and I love the way your photos reflect your view of the world.  You communicate emotion in your work - a think many here will never grasp nor be able to do.  Now get up there and delete that apology.  The fact they don''t agree with you does NOT make them any "righter" than you.  In fact, it makes them wrong in my book.  It''s your art, your execution, by definition you are right.  They can disagree with your "rightness" but it doesn''t make you "wrong". Sorry, I''ll put my righteous indignation away now. I don''t know how you feel about religion and God - if this reflects it or not - but He is one of my best friends.  I highly recommend getting to know Him in whatever way your heart leads you to.  :-)', '2007-09-03 13:32:44.000000', NULL, 0),
